after 99% of throws, throwing it is a great idea.

> It seems to be taking me FOREVER to advance in Hammer with my Mjollnir. 

Different issue I bet.  Each skill slot requires at least one
experience level.  Going from Unskilled to Basic takes 1, from
Basic to Skilled takes 2, and going from Skilled to Expert takes
3 (I think).  If you never advance any skill but war hammer,
you need to get to XP=2 for Basic, XP=4 for Skilled and XP=7
for Expert.  If you have been advancing other weapon classes, it
can take *much* longer.

Consider that each XP level takes exponentially more points
(I think) than the previous one.  You can easily get to the point
where you have to kill 600 dragons and 100 liches just to get to
teh next level, and the level after that might take killing
more monsters than can ever be generated.  By the time you qualify
for the Quest you might never ben able to get another XP level
without potions and such.

Skill slot management is VERY important.

Are you running a Valk?  I like to advance long sword then dagger
then war hammer to Basic.  Dagger then war hammer then long
sword to Skilled.  Dagger then war hammer then long sword to
Expert.  Somewhere in there #twoweapon as well, either after
two of the Skilled or after dagger to Expert.  Expert dagger
rules.

